JVMTI (Java Virtual Machine Tool Interface) is a native interface in Java that allows developers to write agents that can monitor, modify, and manipulate the behavior of the Java virtual machine (JVM). In Android, JVMTI can be used to perform various tasks such as class transformation, method instrumentation, and memory profiling.

Here are some code examples of JVMTI class transformations in Android:

**Example 1: Renaming a class**
```java
// Load the JVMTI agent library
System.loadLibrary("jvmti_agent");

// Define the class transformation function
JNIEXPORT jint JNICALL agent_onclasstransform(JNIEnv *env, jobject jclass) {
    // Get the class object
    jclass clazz = env->FindClass("com/example/MyClass");

    // Rename the class
    env->SetClassName(clazz, "com/example/MyRenamedClass");

    return JNI_OK;
}
```
In this example, the `agent_onclasstransform` function is called when a class is loaded. The function renames the class from "com.example.MyClass" to "com.example.MyRenamedClass".

**Example 2: Adding a method to a class**
```java
// Load the JVMTI agent library
System.loadLibrary("jvmti_agent");

// Define the class transformation function
JNIEXPORT jint JNICALL agent_onclasstransform(JNIEnv *env, jobject jclass) {
    // Get the class object
    jclass clazz = env->FindClass("com/example/MyClass");

    // Define the new method
    jmethodID mid = env->GetMethodID(clazz, "newMethod", "()V");

    // Add the new method to the class
    env->DeclareMethod(mid);

    return JNI_OK;
}
```
In this example, the `agent_onclasstransform` function is called when a class is loaded. The function defines a new method "newMethod" in the class and adds it to the class.

**Example 3: Modifying the method signature of a class**
```java
// Load the JVMTI agent library
System.loadLibrary("jvmti_agent");

// Define the class transformation function
JNIEXPORT jint JNICALL agent_onclasstransform(JNIEnv *env, jobject jclass) {
    // Get the class object
    jclass clazz = env->FindClass("com/example/MyClass");

    // Get the method object
    jmethodID mid = env->GetMethodID(clazz, "myMethod", "()V");

    // Modify the method signature
    env->GetMethodID(clazz, "myMethod", "(II)V");

    return JNI_OK;
}
```
In this example, the `agent_onclasstransform` function is called when a class is loaded. The function gets the method object of the class and modifies its signature. In this case, the method signature is changed from "(())V" to "(II)V".

**Example 4: Instrumenting a method**
```java
// Load the JVMTI agent library
System.loadLibrary("jvmti_agent");

// Define the method instrumentation function
JNIEXPORT jint JNICALL agent_onmethodinstrument(JNIEnv *env, jobject jclass, jmethodID mid) {
    // Get the method object
    jmethodID originalMid = env->GetMethodID(clazz, "myMethod", "(II)V");

    // Instrument the method
    env->CreateInstrumentation(originalMid, "myInstrumentedMethod", "()V");

    return JNI_OK;
